<title>USA: US Treasury's 30-yr bond yield seen at 6.64 pct.</title>
<headline>US Treasury's 30-yr bond yield seen at 6.64 pct.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Treasury's auction of $10.0 billion in 10-year notes on Thursday is expected to produce an average yield near 6.64 percent, dealers said.</p>
<p>At 1252 EST/1752 GMT, the 30-year bonds were quoted at 6.625 percent in when-issued trade.</p>
<p>The bidding deadline for the notes is 1300 EST/1800 GMT and results are expected around 1345 EST/1845 GMT.</p>
<p>-- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1679</p>
</text>
